│ context provided (specifically the           │
│ get_code_around_line output) and the issue   │
│ description. The core problem is that when   │
│ keyword-only arguments with defaults are     │
│ used in simple template tags, incorrect      │
│ error messages are raised. This stems from   │
│ how kwargs is handled and how the tag        │
│ attempts to access keyword arguments. The    │
│ error messages are misleading, suggesting    │
│ unexpected keyword arguments when multiple   │
│ keyword arguments are provided.              │
│                                              │
│ The fix involves modifying the               │
│ register_simple_tag function to correctly    │
│ handle multiple keyword arguments and        │
│ provide a more informative error message.    │
│ Specifically, we need to ensure that the tag │
│ correctly identifies when multiple keyword   │
│ arguments are provided and raise an          │
│ appropriate error.                           │
│                                              │
│ Here's the patch:                            │
│                                              │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃              modification 1              ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  [file]django/template/loader/lib/template.  │
│  [/file]                                     │
│  [original]def register_simple_tag(self,     │
│  name, **signature):                         │
│      """Register a simple tag."""            │
